<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:26Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Is Iran headed to war or peace after Mecca alliance meeting?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a3279be22e5c6655d8f26cb67f0f70830893102ef42aad04dae0645476771f4</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256--9ef674df50a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia, Pakistan and Turkey have taken their latest peace push directly to Tehran. Officially, it was to avert a new military escalation, but their diplomatic outreach can also be seen as a warning to Iran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Cyclone Arnab turns deadly after landfall</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2e3e319c509c1137a7faee4b553c9fb827a1a2a09c0e3d36d98138b54d170ea</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T04:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-cyclone-arnab-turns-deadly-after-landfall/live-79782323--51b97fb16b83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-cyclone-arnab-turns-deadly-after-landfall/live-79782323?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cyclone Arnab killed at least three people in Andhra Pradesh after making landfall earlier today. Also, a new report says India is paying a steep economic cost over heat. Follow live.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mbappe apologizes as Chinese sponsors drop him and TV broadcasts are halted over Mao dictator remark</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:deb0d7f427e06acb8b849dae4037a3a82357cf908fe03f35659ceb76cbe483bb</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T16:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mbappe-apologizes-as-chinese-sponsors-drop-him-and-tv-broadcasts-are-halted-over-mao-dictator-remark/a-79779831--140a68dc18a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mbappe-apologizes-as-chinese-sponsors-drop-him-and-tv-broadcasts-are-halted-over-mao-dictator-remark/a-79779831?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French soccer star Kylian Mbappe has apologized after apparently referring to Mao Zedong as a dictator. Chinese sponsors have dropped him, while state television has suspended Spanish league broadcasts.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar: Is the US undermining the EU's diplomatic blockade?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9113a8cf9acd66e50daaffd967ea8fdd5fa7ae2acbf5f1d61677df8b26f35c91</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T15:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-is-the-us-undermining-the-eu-s-diplomatic-blockade/a-79778863--db2dea3e5776.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-is-the-us-undermining-the-eu-s-diplomatic-blockade/a-79778863?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With the US reopening talks with Myanmar's military-backed government, and several Southeast Asian countries restarting diplomatic contacts, the EU is facing uncomfortable questions about its own boycott of the junta.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will elections in Israel change its Iran approach?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e62592511b46894eb26c331111da9f059d08e18d792f188df6932faa2edbf0f</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122--d46c291154a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls, the country's conflict with Iran casts a long shadow over the ballot box. But any leadership changes in Israel may not be enough to shake up its grand strategy on Tehran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Arunachal sees fresh violence over proposed dam</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a26ab38374674b7bc4f9734dc248ce557d0a277ea90ed19e11cacc71eb598b48</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T07:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-arunachal-sees-fresh-violence-over-proposed-dam/live-79771650--d59bfea6f557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-arunachal-sees-fresh-violence-over-proposed-dam/live-79771650?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More violence erupted in India's northeastern state of Arunachal Pradesh over proposed hydroelectric projects that locals are protesting. Also, India's top court will hear pleas against the poll body chief.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz in Asia as security issues loom large</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60042dbe11d260b66f89bb8d58df4bae3d4bd13a2d863c7638844bc169a63bc9</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-in-asia-as-security-issues-loom-large/a-79764065--009b584587c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-in-asia-as-security-issues-loom-large/a-79764065?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz will be meeting the leaders of Singapore, Japan and South Korea as Germany seeks to adjust its foreign policy to rising uncertainty and threats to global supply chains.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Steinmeier in China: A major state visit in uncertain times</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1eda7986ab9105c9e2651c1b396630cb9ac31bedca86bee86cf0152b67562995</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/steinmeier-in-china-a-major-state-visit-in-uncertain-times/a-79764205--23bd9ee47a5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/steinmeier-in-china-a-major-state-visit-in-uncertain-times/a-79764205?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Frank-Walter Steinmeier is traveling to China on a state visit in a period of political and economic uncertainty. Germany is seeking alternative partners in the region but also wants good ties with Beijing.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>North Korean workers treated as 'slaves' at Russian drone factory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb241807f107024ba74b3825f2aa8948b0e8328bc317d645f513c3383d45ef0b</id><updated>2026-10-28T21:12:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T17:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory/a-79710877--83771c04f78a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory/a-79710877?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report reveals the plight of North Korean workers at a drone factory in Russia. It also raised concerns that Pyongyang could gain hands-on knowledge of advanced weapons systems through the workers it sends there.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
